---
/**
 * Public Privacy Policy page.
 *
 * Migrated from NiceGUI @ui.page('/privacy') (which read paddle_page.PRIVACY).
 * In P3-B we deleted the NiceGUI mount; this Astro page replaces it.
 *
 * Content ownership: the user (castor maintainer) should review with a
 * lawyer before shipping. The text below is the upstream beaverhabits
 * text with product references rebranded to Castor; legal substance
 * is unchanged.
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/PublicLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Castor" description="How Castor handles your data.">
  <main id="main" class="castor-page">
    <PageHeader title="Privacy Policy" back="/" subtitle="Effective Date: 2026-09-22" />

    <article
      class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-card p-6 sm:p-10 prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none"
      style="border-radius: var(--castor-card-radius); padding: var(--castor-card-padding);"
    >
      <h2>Introduction</h2>
      <p>
        Castor is a self-hostable habit tracker. When you use Castor, your data lives
        on the instance run by your administrator (most often: yourself). Your privacy
        is important; this Privacy Policy outlines how data is collected, used, and
        protected.
      </p>

      <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>Castor stores the following information to provide the service:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Account information</strong>: email address, display name, hashed
          password, and (optionally) WebAuthn / passkey public keys.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Habit data</strong>: habits you create, completion ticks, notes,
          streak metadata, and tags.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Private Circles</strong>: if you create or join a circle, the
          shared habits and members are visible to other members of that circle
          according to the visibility you select.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Audit log</strong>: every login, password reset, and administrative
          action is recorded with timestamp and IP for security review.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
      <p>Data is used only to provide the service:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Authenticate you and protect your account.</li>
        <li>Store and display your habits, streaks, and notes.</li>
        <li>Share habits with Private Circle members at the visibility level you choose.</li>
        <li>Detect abuse, support audit requirements, and notify you of security events.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sharing Your Information</h2>
      <p>
        Castor does not sell, trade, or transfer personal information to third parties.
        Data may be shared only:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>With other members of a Private Circle, at the visibility you selected when sharing the habit.</li>
        <li>With service providers used by your instance administrator (e.g. SMTP for password-reset emails). These providers receive only the data needed to perform the service.</li>
        <li>When required by law.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Security of Your Information</h2>
      <p>
        Castor implements layered security:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Passwords are hashed with bcrypt.</li>
        <li>Sessions use httpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax cookies with a 24-hour lifetime.</li>
        <li>WebAuthn / passkey authentication uses challenge-based, origin-bound assertions.</li>
        <li>Logout bumps a server-side token version, invalidating all outstanding bearer tokens.</li>
        <li>POST endpoints enforce Origin and Referer header checks to mitigate CSRF.</li>
        <li>HTTP responses include HSTS, CSP, X-Frame-Options, and other security headers.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        No method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is 100% secure;
        we continuously improve defenses but cannot guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
      <p>
        You can request account deletion at any time from
        <a href="/settings">Settings → Account → Delete account</a>. Deletion removes your
        account, habits, notes, audit log entries, and circle memberships. Audit logs
        may retain anonymized action records for security review.
      </p>

      <h2>Your Rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access, rectify, or delete your personal information.</li>
        <li>Export your data at any time from <a href="/export">Settings → Export</a>.</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent and stop using the service.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        The instance administrator may update this Privacy Policy. Significant changes
        will be communicated to users via email.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this Privacy Policy should be directed to your instance
        administrator. For open-source licensing questions, see the project's
        GitHub repository.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
